From 770841f9600e174cdfa9dbdd8d69055dd2177fcb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman Fries <baracoder@googlemail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 14:12:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm: Initial support for async page flips

Backport of Smithay/smithay#1948 ("Initial support for DRM async page
flip v2", head f8a8f0fa) onto rev f581531d, for ionwl's tearing control.

`DrmCompositor::render_frame` takes the desired `PresentationMode`. A
frame asking for `Async` is flipped with `PageFlipFlags::ASYNC` when only
the primary plane changed, compatibly with the previous frame; overlay
planes are not assigned for it. A rejected async flip is retried in sync
and not attempted again until the primary plane's properties change.
The device's async-flip capability (`DRM_CAP_ATOMIC_ASYNC_PAGE_FLIP`, or
`DRM_CAP_ASYNC_PAGE_FLIP` on legacy) gates the flag.

Deviations from the PR:
- `frame_submitted` keeps returning `Option<U>` (the PR's switch to an
  `EmptyFrame` error is unrelated to async flips).
- `DrmSurface::supports_async_page_flips` lets the compositor skip the
  async attempt on devices without the capability, so the presentation
  mode it reports for the pending frame is the one actually used.
- The anvil changes are left out.
